WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.500
Surgical Skills Demonstration: One-Handed Square Knot Suture Technique.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:15.000
Hold the post strand under moderate tension with your non-dominant hand while manipulating the loop strand.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:23.500
First throw: Wrap the working strand over the index finger, forming an anterior loop around the post.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:32.000
Pass the tail through the loop using the index fingertip, ensuring the throw is laid completely square and flat.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Second throw: Reverse the wrap by using the middle and ring fingers to cross behind the post strand.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:47.500
Pull the second throw down flat against the initial throw, securing the square knot without slip.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:53.021
Verify knot symmetry and tension across the surgical wound margin to prevent tissue strangulation.
